-- title:
--   Socle of a finite complete intersection is generated by det g
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, $n$ a natural number, and let $R = k[[X_0,\dots,X_{n-1}]] =$ `MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k` be the ring of formal power series in $n$ variables over $k$. Let $g$ be an $n \times n$ matrix with entries in $R$, and let $f : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to R$ be a family of power series such that $f_i = \sum_j g_{ij} X_j$ for every index $i$, where $X_j$ denotes the $j$-th variable. Write $I = (f_0,\dots,f_{n-1})$ for the ideal of $R$ generated by the range of $f$, and assume that the quotient $A = R/I$ is finite as a $k$-module, i.e. finite-dimensional as a $k$-vector space. The conclusion is twofold: first, the image of $\det g$ under the quotient map $R \to A$ is nonzero; second, for every ideal $J$ of $A$ with $J \neq \bot$, the image of $\det g$ belongs to $J$. Thus the class of $\det g$ generates the unique minimal nonzero ideal of $A$, which is therefore one-dimensional over $k$. The proof cites [`Ideal.colon_span_eq_sup_span_det_of_isWeaklyRegular`](thm.html#Ideal.colon_span_eq_sup_span_det_of_isWeaklyRegular), which computes, for a commutative ring $P$, sequences $x, f$ and a matrix $g$ with $f_i = \sum_j g_{ij}x_j$ and a weakly regular sequence inside $(f)$, the colon ideals $(f) : (x) = (f) + (\det g)$ and $(f) : (\det g) = (x)$.
--
--   This identifies the socle of a zero-dimensional complete intersection $k[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]/(f_1,\dots,f_n)$ with the line spanned by the class of the determinant of a matrix of coefficients, a lemma of Tate used in the de Smit–Rubin–Schoof treatment of the Wiles–Lenstra numerical criterion for complete intersections. It is used in the commutative-algebra part of the modularity-lifting argument, being cited by [`AlgHom.bijective_and_exists_presentation_of_length_cotangent_le`](thm.html#AlgHom.bijective_and_exists_presentation_of_length_cotangent_le), [`Algebra.bijective_rTensor_dual_bezoutian_of_isAlgClosed`](thm.html#Algebra.bijective_rTensor_dual_bezoutian_of_isAlgClosed) and [`MvPowerSeries.exists_bijective_compr2_mul_of_finite`](thm.html#MvPowerSeries.exists_bijective_compr2_mul_of_finite).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPowerSeries_quotient_mk_det_mem_of_ne_bot.lean

import Mathlib.RingTheory.Regular.RegularSequence
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Colon
import Mathlib.RingTheory.MvPowerSeries.Basic
import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Determinant.Basic

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

universe u

theorem MvPowerSeries.quotient_mk_det_mem_of_ne_bot
    {k : Type u} [Field k] {n : ℕ} (g : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k))
    (f : Fin n → MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k) (hf : ∀ i, f i = ∑ j, g i j * MvPowerSeries.X j)
    [Module.Finite k (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range f))] :
    Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span (Set.range f)) g.det ≠ 0 ∧
      ∀ J : Ideal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range f)), J ≠ ⊥ →
        Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span (Set.range f)) g.det ∈ J := by sorry
